# oracle: pair_style hybrid/overlay eam/fs coul/ctip 0.30 12.0 (examples/streitz/in.ctip) on a 216-atom subset (3x3x3 NiO cells of data.ctip), fix qeq/ctip 1 12.0 1.0e-8 100 coul/ctip cdamp 0.30 maxrepeat 10, NVE 10 steps
# native: installed /home/roy/.local/bin/lmp (b332f28; EXTRA-PAIR, QEQ, KSPACE, MANYBODY). Measured max relative error vs native:
#   thermo 5.9e-9 (ke, step 2), per-atom charges 2.1e-9, positions 8e-10, forces 2e-8, velocities 3e-7 (positions, forces and
#   velocities scaled by max(1,|x|) as tests/oracleHarness.ts does; its atomrel default is 1e-6, so this file passes it).
#   The same case with fix tolerance 1e-12 agrees to 3e-13 everywhere, so the difference is the CG stop point at 1e-8: the
#   charge matrix is roundoff-sensitive (reversing the pair summation order moves the engine step-0 charges by 9e-10).
#   Target 1e-8 relative: met for thermo and charges; forces and velocities are not met (2e-8, 3e-7). f_1 (CG count) agrees at the printed rows
#   (steps 0, 2, ..., 10); on the unprinted steps 1 and 7 the engine's count is one lower than native's (23 vs 24, 7 vs 8).
# oracle-potentials: NiO.eam.fs NiO.ctip
# oracle-inputs: w140ct_ctip.data
# oracle-files: w140ct_ctip_q.dump
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-8 abs=1e-10 filerel=1e-8
units           metal
atom_style      charge
boundary        p p p
read_data       w140ct_ctip.data
pair_style      hybrid/overlay eam/fs coul/ctip 0.30 12.0
pair_coeff      * * eam/fs NiO.eam.fs Ni O
pair_coeff      * * coul/ctip NiO.ctip Ni O
fix             1 all qeq/ctip 1 12.0 1.0e-8 100 coul/ctip cdamp 0.30 maxrepeat 10
variable        dx atom 0.04*sin(1.3*x+0.7*y)
variable        dy atom 0.04*cos(0.9*y-0.4*z)
variable        dz atom 0.04*sin(1.1*z+0.5*x)
displace_atoms  all move v_dx v_dy v_dz units box
variable        vx atom 0.01*sin(id)
variable        vy atom 0.01*cos(2*id)
variable        vz atom 0.01*sin(3*id)
velocity        all set v_vx v_vy v_vz
timestep        0.001
fix             2 all nve
thermo_style    custom step pe ecoul evdwl ke f_1
thermo_modify   format float %.15g norm no
thermo          2
run             10
write_dump      all custom w140ct_ctip_q.dump id q modify format float %.15g sort id
